# Vendor property contexts. Every entry verified against
# device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr (same branch) for conflicting claims.

# ARM's EGL config table, read by libGLES_mali r54p1 in EVERY process that
# touches EGL. Set in configs/properties/vendor.prop (39 keys, [C] values).
# Unlabelled these fall to vendor_default_prop, which no app domain can
# read -- the driver then sees them as unset and rebuilds a broken table,
# and property-read refusals are dontaudit'd so no denial sweep can ever
# catch it (only the functional EGL floor gate can).
#
# vendor_mtk_gpu_prop needs no new grant (attribute-mediated get_prop via
# mtk_core_property_type, invisible to name greps). The prefix
# ro.vendor.arm. matches Samsung's usage on the same SoC and also covers
# ro.vendor.arm.gralloc.* keys. Corroboration, not conflict: Advan stock's
# own vendor_property_contexts line 318 carries this exact prefix->type
# mapping, so the built image agrees with stock about the label.
#
# This class cannot be live-tested here (contexts are read before
# post-fs-data) -- it must be proven in a BUILD, then by the camera EGL
# path on hardware.
ro.vendor.arm.                              u:object_r:vendor_mtk_gpu_prop:s0
